From: grimtickle-overlay (local)
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdns3: sky1: fix unchecked mode-strap, preset ordering, and clk cleanup in drd_init

Four related defects in cdnsp_sky1_drd_init()/sky1_usb_clk_disable_all(),
found during pre-trial review of 0150-0162:

1. sky1_set_mode_by_id(data->dev, MODE_STRAP_OTG) returned an int but its
   result was discarded. A regmap_update_bits() failure here silently left
   the controller strapped in the wrong USB mode while probe reported
   success. Check it and fail the same way the other required steps do.

2. axi_base and the mode-strap syscon were being written/updated *before*
   reset_control_deassert(data->preset) in the original patch, while the
   surrounding code and the 0153 commit message both document that
   register access must happen after preset is released (the same pattern
   already used for the D_XEC_* writes immediately below). Move both
   calls after the preset-deassert success check, consistent with that
   documented ordering and with every other register access in this
   function.

3. The err_assert_preset cleanup path called reset_control_assert(data->preset)
   without checking its return value, so a cleanup failure during an
   already-failing probe was silently swallowed. Capture it and log it
   (without replacing the original error being propagated, since the
   original failure is still the more relevant one to report).

4. sky1_usb_clk_disable_all() left cix_usb_clks[] populated with disabled
   clk pointers. A subsequent call to this function (e.g. a retried
   drd_init() on a role-switch or resume path) would call
   clk_disable_unprepare() a second time on an already-unprepared clk,
   which is unsafe. NULL each pointer after disabling it so a repeat call
   is a safe no-op, matching the existing NULL-out pattern already used
   in sky1_usb_clk_enable_all()'s own error path.

No functional change to the normal (all-steps-succeed) boot path besides
the axi_base/mode-strap register writes now happening a few instructions
later in program order, after preset is confirmed released.
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
@@ -150,8 +150,15 @@
 
 	dev_info(dev, "---------sky1_usb_clk_disable_all----------\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * NULL out each pointer after disabling it so a later retry (e.g. a
+	 * failed drd_init() calling this again, or suspend/resume racing a
+	 * role-switch retry) cannot double-disable an already-unprepared clk.
+	 * clk_disable_unprepare(NULL) is a safe no-op.
+	 */
 	for (i = 0; i < CIX_USB_CLK_NUM; i++) {
 		clk_disable_unprepare(cix_usb_clks[i]);
+		cix_usb_clks[i] = NULL;
 	}
 };
 
@@ -325,15 +332,26 @@
 			"cdnsp_sky1_drd_init: failed to enable clocks: %d\n", ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
-	writel(CIX_USB_AXI_WR_CACHE_VALUE, data->axi_base);
-	sky1_set_mode_by_id(data->dev, MODE_STRAP_OTG);
-
 	ret = reset_control_deassert(data->preset);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(data->dev,
 			"cdnsp_sky1_drd_init: failed to deassert preset: %d\n", ret);
 		goto err_disable_clk;
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * axi_base and the mode-strap syscon are only accessible once preset
+	 * is released, so these must come after reset_control_deassert()
+	 * above, not before it.
+	 */
+	writel(CIX_USB_AXI_WR_CACHE_VALUE, data->axi_base);
+	ret = sky1_set_mode_by_id(data->dev, MODE_STRAP_OTG);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(data->dev,
+			"cdnsp_sky1_drd_init: failed to set OTG mode strap: %d\n", ret);
+		goto err_assert_preset;
+	}
+
 	if (data->u3_disable) {
 		dev_info(data->dev, "[%s:%d]disable u3 port\n", __func__, __LINE__);
 		writel(D_XEC_CFG_3XPORT_MODE_VALUE, (void *)(data->device_base)
@@ -517,7 +535,14 @@
 	 * clocks enabled above to leave the device in a fully-quiesced,
 	 * known state rather than a partially clocked/programmed one.
 	 */
-	reset_control_assert(data->preset);
+	{
+		int cleanup_ret = reset_control_assert(data->preset);
+
+		if (cleanup_ret)
+			dev_err(data->dev,
+				"cdnsp_sky1_drd_init: failed to reassert preset during cleanup: %d\n",
+				cleanup_ret);
+	}
 err_disable_clk:
 	sky1_usb_clk_disable_all(data->dev);
 	return ret;
